---
import MainLayout from '../../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<MainLayout
  title="OpsTower | Phillip Pieterse"
  description="OpsTower is an operational intelligence platform built to improve visibility, reporting truth, and operational decision-making."
>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main class="page-shell">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Platform case study</div>
        <h1 class="page-title">OpsTower</h1>
        <p class="page-copy">
          OpsTower is an operational intelligence platform built to improve visibility,
          reporting truth, intervention speed, and control across complex live operations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="surface case-study-hero">
        <div>
          <div class="badge-row">
            <span class="badge live">Flagship platform</span>
            <span class="tag">Next.js</span>
            <span class="tag">TypeScript</span>
            <span class="tag">Prisma</span>
            <span class="tag">PostgreSQL</span>
          </div>

          <h2>Built for visibility, control, and operational decision-making.</h2>
          <p class="detail-copy">
            OpsTower brings operational truth into one platform: live KPIs, exception handling,
            admin controls, reporting surfaces, route optimization workflows, and transport
            monitoring tools that help teams move from raw signals to action faster.
          </p>

          <div class="detail-grid compact-metrics">
            <article class="detail-card metric-card">
              <div class="detail-label">Role</div>
              <div class="detail-value">Platform design + frontend + reporting</div>
            </article>
            <article class="detail-card metric-card">
              <div class="detail-label">Focus</div>
              <div class="detail-value">Operational clarity</div>
            </article>
            <article class="detail-card metric-card">
              <div class="detail-label">Outcome</div>
              <div class="detail-value">Faster follow-up</div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-preview contain-frame">
          <img
            src="/images/projects/opstower/last-mile-views.png"
            alt="OpsTower dashboard view cards"
          />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">Core strengths</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">What the platform delivers</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="highlight-grid">
          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Live operational visibility</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Surfaces current package state, active risk, reporting views, and intervention
              areas in a way teams can act on quickly.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Admin and control surfaces</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Provides management tools for worker visibility, sync health, operational
              settings, and shared control points across the platform.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Route optimization foundation</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Creates space for route planning, optimized sequencing, visual QA, and stronger
              decision support for last-mile execution.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Transport control direction</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Extends the platform into truck movement visibility, checkpoint tracking, delay
              intelligence, and transport intervention workflows.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">Impact</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Why it matters operationally</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">
            OpsTower is designed to reduce blind spots, improve operational follow-up, and
            give teams a clearer view of what needs attention right now.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="highlight-grid">
          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Improves live visibility</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Gives operators clearer visibility into package state, pending work, and
              operational breakdowns.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Surfaces risk earlier</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Helps expose operational risks and intervention queues sooner, before they turn
              into larger failures.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Reduces switching</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Brings visibility, controls, and reporting closer together so teams spend less
              time jumping between disconnected views.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="highlight-card">
            <h3>Creates a stronger platform base</h3>
            <p class="detail-copy">
              Establishes the foundation for route optimization and transport control as part
              of a broader operational system.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">Screenshots</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Inside OpsTower</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">
            These views show the platform from both sides: operational monitoring for action,
            and control surfaces for management.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="screenshot-grid">
          <figure class="screenshot-card screenshot-frame">
            <img
              src="/images/projects/opstower/live-overview.png"
              alt="OpsTower live overview screenshot"
            />
            <figcaption>
              Live overview focused on current package state, pending work, and operational
              breakdowns.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="screenshot-card screenshot-frame">
            <img
              src="/images/projects/opstower/control-tower.png"
              alt="OpsTower control tower screenshot"
            />
            <figcaption>
              Control tower entry point with navigation into live views, reporting,
              exceptions, and admin spaces.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="screenshot-card screenshot-frame">
            <img
              src="/images/projects/opstower/admin-controls.png"
              alt="OpsTower admin controls screenshot"
            />
            <figcaption>
              Administrative control surfaces for operational truth, settings, and access to
              management tools.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="screenshot-card screenshot-frame">
            <img
              src="/images/projects/opstower/worker-center.png"
              alt="OpsTower worker center screenshot"
            />
            <figcaption>
              Worker center with scheduler controls, sync run status, timing, and operational
              health indicators.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="surface">
          <div class="section-head">
            <div class="eyebrow">Platform direction</div>
            <h2 class="section-title">OpsTower is growing beyond a dashboard.</h2>
            <p class="section-copy">
              The next evolution of OpsTower includes focused modules for route optimization
              and transport control, expanding the platform from visibility into planning and
              intervention.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="primary-button" href="/projects/opstower-route-optimization">
              Route Optimization
            </a>
            <a class="ghost-button" href="/projects/opstower-transport-control">
              Transport Control
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</MainLayout>